[For "white"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Start "london-englund 2.dxe5"]
[Name "The Englund: 2...Bc5"]

2... Bc5 { Aims at f2 at once, and plans to win the pawn back with ...d6 or ...f6. }
3. Nf3 { Develops and guards e5. }
3... d6 { Black offers a second pawn to open lines. }
4. Bf4 { The bishop defends e5 again from its usual square. Taking on d6 also works, but it gives Black's pieces the open lines they want. }
4... Ne7
5. e3 { Blocks the c5 bishop's diagonal and frees White's own bishop. White is a healthy pawn up. [%cal Ge3f2] } *
